==English==

===Etymology===
From {{affix|en|field|-s-|man}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|EN-AU ck1 fieldsman.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-fieldsman.ogg|a=AU}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|fieldsmen}}

# {{lb|en|cricket|chiefly|Australia|dated|_|in|_|UK}} [[fielder]]
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=March 19, 2009|author=AAP|title=India 4-278 at stumps|work=Herald Sun|url=http://www.news.com.au/heraldsun/story/0,21985,25209493-11088,00.html
|passage=The batsmen took an easy single as the ball approached the '''fieldsman''' but Gambhir called for a second on the throw and Franklin uprooted the non-striker's stumps.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1922|author=Ernest Raymond|title=Tell England|chapter=|edition=|url=http://www.gutenberg.org/etext/15033
|passage=Radley pulled it, as a great laugh went up, to the very spot from which the '''fieldsman''' had been removed.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1920|author=Various|title=Punch, or the London Charivari, Vol. 159, July 14th, 1920|chapter=|edition=|url=http://www.gutenberg.org/etext/16592
|passage=I timed it successfully, and had no doubt of having added four to my score, when, to my astonishment, I saw a '''fieldsman''' running from the direction of the hedge.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1905|author=Norman Gale|title=More Cricket Songs|chapter=|edition=|url=http://www.gutenberg.org/etext/13167
|passage=Watch the flying '''fieldsman''', Keen to save the fourer, Gallop past the wooden box Sacred to the scorer!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1873|author=Various|title=The World's Greatest Books, Vol VI.|chapter=|edition=|url=http://www.gutenberg.org/etext/11180
|passage=William Grey, 1; Samuel Long, 2; James Brown, 3; George and John Simmons, one capital, the other so-so--an uncertain hitter, but a good '''fieldsman''', 5; Joel Brent, excellent, 6; Ben Appleton--here was a little pause, for Ben's abilities at cricket were not completely ascertained, but then he was a good fellow, so full of fun and waggery!}}

